Package: displaceR
Title: Run the 'DISPLACE' Fisheries Simulator from R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pol", "Carbo Mestre", email = "polcarbo@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = "Author of this R interface only, not of DISPLACE"),
    person("Francois", "Bastardie", email = "fba@aqua.dtu.dk",
           role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "Author and copyright holder of the DISPLACE simulator
                      (https://github.com/frabas/DISPLACE_GUI), which this
                      package runs but does not modify"),
    person(family = "DTU Aqua", role = "cph",
           comment = "Copyright holder of the DISPLACE simulator"))
Description: An R interface to 'DISPLACE', the dynamic, individual-based model
    for spatial fishing planning and effort displacement developed by Francois
    Bastardie and colleagues at DTU Aqua and described in Bastardie, Nielsen
    and Miethe (2014) <doi:10.1139/cjfas-2013-0126>. All of the science is
    theirs: this package contains no model code and implements no model
    behaviour. It installs a prebuilt 'DISPLACE' binary, writes and validates
    its input files, runs it, and reads its 'SQLite' and text outputs back into
    data frames, so that existing case studies can be driven from R on Linux,
    macOS and Windows. Modelled on the 'r4ss' / 'cmdstanr' pattern where the
    backend is installed separately into a user directory. Please cite the
    'DISPLACE' publications, not this package, when publishing results.
License: GPL-2
URL: https://github.com/pcarbomestre/displaceR,
    https://github.com/frabas/DISPLACE_GUI,
    https://displace-project.org/
BugReports: https://github.com/pcarbomestre/displaceR/issues
Note: Report problems with this R interface at the BugReports address above.
    Problems with the DISPLACE model itself belong with the DISPLACE project.
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    DBI,
    RSQLite,
    digest,
    jsonlite,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
SystemRequirements: The DISPLACE simulator, which runs on Linux, macOS and
    Windows. On 64-bit Linux install_displace() downloads a prebuilt binary at
    runtime; on macOS and Windows install upstream's package and point the
    DISPLACE_BINARY environment variable at the simulator. No compiler or CMake
    is required on the target machine.
